        "theme":  "Platforms",
        "summary":  "Amazon Bedrock AgentCore is an agentic AI platform that orchestrates specialized agents — intake, infrastructure-as-code generation, governance, and SRE — across cloud migration workflows, reducing the manual translation work that historically caused delays and inconsistency. Unlike most hyperscaler migration tools, AgentCore is designed to support hybrid and multicloud environments by accepting multiple agent frameworks, foundation models, and external APIs beyond AWS infrastructure. The author maintains healthy skepticism about vendor lock-in, recommending enterprises verify how well AgentCore handles Azure-native and GCP-native patterns before committing.",
        "execSummary":  "AWS has moved beyond AI as a migration chatbot and embedded agentic orchestration directly into cloud migration programs via Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, automating the most repetitive translation layers — application intake, IaC generation, compliance reporting, and post-cutover SRE monitoring. For CIOs managing multi-hundred-application migration backlogs, the platform\u0027s IaC agent alone could dramatically compress delivery timelines. The key caveat is that AgentCore remains an AWS-managed service, so enterprises should explicitly test its handling of non-AWS workloads before adopting it as a platform-agnostic migration layer. SRE agents should be configured with recommendation-only mode — never autonomous production changes — to preserve human accountability in cutover decisions.",
