        "source":  "Microsoft AI Blog",
        "url":  "https://news.microsoft.com/signal/articles/how-to-build-an-ai-agent-guide/",
        "date":  "2026-08-10",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Microsoft\u0027s Signal blog presents a five-step framework for building AI agents using Microsoft 365 Copilot, targeting business users with minimal technical expertise. The guide emphasizes starting with a concrete problem, evaluating existing prebuilt agents, and using natural language to describe agent functionality before connecting data sources. A key distinction drawn is that agents \u0027can also take action\u0027 unlike traditional chatbots, with examples including automated security incident response and weekly status reports.",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprise leaders considering agent deployments should note Microsoft\u0027s push to democratize agent-building via natural-language interfaces in M365 Copilot, significantly lowering the technical bar for line-of-business teams. The five-step framework — problem definition, prebuilt evaluation, natural-language specification, data connection, and iterative testing — provides a repeatable pattern for non-technical stakeholders. The implication: agent adoption no longer requires dedicated engineering resources, accelerating the pace at which business units can self-serve automation. Caveat: governance frameworks and scope controls need to be established before widespread adoption to prevent runaway agent actions across enterprise systems.",
