        "summary":  "Microsoft\u0027s startup blog profiles Maven, which uses AI agents built on Azure to shift enterprise customer service from deflection to resolution. Unlike traditional chatbots that route issues away, Maven\u0027s agents take action to fully resolve customer problems within the same interaction. The piece illustrates the broader enterprise shift from cost-reduction AI to value-generation AI in customer experience functions.",
        "execSummary":  "The Maven case study is a signal that enterprise AI in customer service is evolving past deflection metrics toward full resolution rates — a materially different value proposition for CX leaders. Agents that resolve rather than deflect can simultaneously reduce support costs and lift customer satisfaction, addressing a long-standing tension in support economics. For enterprise leaders, the implication is that AI agent ROI models need to be rebuilt around resolution rates and CSAT, not just containment percentages. Caveat: true resolution requires deep system integration and robust fallback to human agents for edge cases — organizations should plan integration scope carefully before promising customers resolution-grade experiences.",
