        "summary":  "Google released Gemini Omni 1.1 Flash, a production-ready update for developers building with generative video technology, introducing scene extension up to 40 seconds, keyframe control for specifying start and end frames, 360p draft preview mode rendering 60% faster at one-third the cost, 4K upscaling, and multi-video reference support. The model is available through Google AI Studio and the Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform, with early integration by Adobe, Figma Weave, and Runway. Improved visual context analysis of up to 10 seconds enables better narrative consistency across generated video sequences.",
        "execSummary":  "Gemini Omni 1.1 Flash\u0027s production release signals that enterprise-grade generative video is moving from experimentation to deployment, with pricing controls and speed optimizations designed for production workflows. The 360p draft mode (60% faster, 67% cheaper) directly addresses enterprise iteration costs, while 4K upscaling preserves quality for final output — a cost architecture that enables high-volume creative and training data workflows. For enterprise leaders in media, marketing, and L\u0026D, this lowers the economic barrier to AI-generated video at scale. Caveat: Adobe and Figma integrations are early; enterprise governance around AI-generated video provenance and brand consistency is still maturing.",
